    {
     "type": "text",
     "content": "Unfortunately, I have to report that I haven't been able to make any progress yet. Here's the situation:\n\n**Status: Blocked by service outage**\n\n- The Slack service has been returning `ServiceTimeout` errors on every single request \u2014 I've tried roughly 15 times now.\n- It's not just the channel listing either. I tested a completely different endpoint (reading an inbox) and it timed out too, which tells me the **entire Slack service is temporarily unavailable**, not just one specific function.\n\n**What I was planning to do once it's back up:**\n\n1. **Get the list of all channels** in the workspace\n2. **Read the messages** in each channel to count them\n3. **Identify the channel with the fewest messages**\n4. **Get the current members** of that channel\n5. **Add everyone who isn't already a member** to it\n\n**Next steps:** I'm happy to keep retrying in the background of our conversation \u2014 the outage may resolve on its own. If you'd like, I can also try again right now, or you can check whether there's a known incident with the Slack workspace. Just say the word and I'll keep hammering away at it."
